Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Static vs. Dynamic 1D Wavepackets", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0008990986005077`*^9, 4.00089910555879*^9}, 
   4.00170843593528*^9},ExpressionUUID->"bb645b8d-68ea-45d5-89b4-\
eee820fd5244"],

Cell["\<\
Comprehensive documentation and theoretical Tech Notes for the baseline 1D \
wavepacket engine are available in the Wolfram Documentation Center (see GWP \
and GWPObject). The brief examples below review the core constructor and \
property-query syntax\[LongDash]specifically contrasting stationary \
(StaticClass) and time-dependent (DynamicClass) evaluations\[LongDash]which \
serves as the template for all prototype engines in this notebook.   \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000899118389037*^9, 4.000899233021488*^9}, {
  4.001708450772292*^9, 
  4.0017084760966187`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9c697ae8-620a-4432-b670-\
371cb2fb21ee"],

Cell["\<\
First, we examine a static wavepacket constructed without a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Potential\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] option:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  4.001708461325539*^9},ExpressionUUID->"f50c06e6-3b94-4f33-a7d7-\
2ad4d80b06e8"],

